Security/no-claim proof for WP20:

- Stored app/game session references are required; the contract does not treat
  portal timers or raw UI refresh state as time evidence.
- Running-time and foreground-only modes are separate, so foreground budgets do
  not count background duration.
- Launcher-game candidate sessions are counted only when the target accepts the
  session kind and the policy/session classification matches.
- Bonus time does not extend a budget without approval and audit refs.
- Manual-required and dry-run-only handoff states do not dispatch adapters.
- Restart recovery cannot be claimed without timer refs and recovery audit refs.
- No private process paths, command lines, child content, screenshots, tokens,
  or raw journal/SQLite rows are introduced by this slice.
